course: dictionary
lesson: 2748
title: Disallow: when a rule says no
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: When a referee says a goal does not count, they disallow it. The prefix dis- often means "not", and allow means let something happen, so disallow means to refuse to accept something.
explain: Look at the context. «a disallowed goal» is a goal that was not counted because it broke a rule. The words around it, such as «disappointment» and «a cancelled holiday», show that disallowed is something unhappy that stops you getting what you wanted.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it in. "A goal that was not accepted" still makes sense in the sentence, so you have the right idea. Disallow is a verb, so it changes: disallows, disallowed, disallowing.
fact: Disallow is a verb meaning to officially refuse to accept something.
fact: Disallow usually means refusing something because it broke a rule.
fact: «The goal was disallowed» is the past form, so it means the goal was not counted.
fact: The prefix dis- often means "not", as in dislike and disagree.
fact: Disallow can also mean to not permit something, such as settings that stop certain apps on a computer.
exercise: «The goal was disallowed.» What does disallowed mean here? | Kicked very hard | Scored with a header | *Refused, because it broke a rule | Painted in bright colours
exercise: In disallow, what does the prefix dis- mean? | Again and again | *Not | Under | Very
exercise: Fill in the gap: «Yesterday the referee ___ the goal.» | disallows | disallowing | disallow | *disallowed
test: The computer will disallow the game app. What does this mean? | *It will not permit the app to run | It will give the app a prize | It will make the app louder | It will update the app every hour
test: Which sentence uses disallow correctly? | The goal disallowing was very loud. | Disallowing the sunshine was fun. | *The referee disallowed the goal for offside. | The cake was disallow yesterday.
exam: Which word is closest in meaning to disallow? | Repeat | Accept | Celebrate | *Refuse
